<description>
**Problem:** With a normal `-bind` (but no dedicated onion bind), automatic Tor services can forward incoming connections to the normal P2P listener, where they may be misclassified and inherit IP-based whitelist permissions.

**Fix:** If no dedicated onion bind exists, keep Tor control available for outbound proxy discovery but skip automatic incoming service creation and warn after authentication.
The node starts with its configured listeners (including the default onion listener when no `-bind` is supplied), and Tor control starts only after those listeners have been opened successfully.

Affected nodes need a concrete `-bind=<addr>:<port>=onion` to restore incoming Tor connections.

Wildcard onion binds are rejected at startup when `-listenonion` is enabled, while their classification with `-listenonion=0` remains outside this change.
</description>

<commits>
a9fea0bda8 refactor/test: prepare Tor bind handling and tests

Prepare bind initialization and the mock-controller fixture to check explicit onion service targets and peer permissions without changing node behavior.

Co-authored-by: HouseOfHufflepuff <ahrens@gmail.com>
Co-authored-by: JP <jeanpablo.jp@hotmail.com>

b9c02b46fb test: characterize automatic Tor service creation

Record that automatic service creation forwards to a shared P2P bind, that wildcard onion binds start normally, and that Tor control starts even when binding fails.
Check outbound proxy discovery alongside incoming service creation so the fixes can preserve outgoing Tor connections.

Co-authored-by: HouseOfHufflepuff <ahrens@gmail.com>
Co-authored-by: JP <jeanpablo.jp@hotmail.com>

448db280e3 init: start Tor control after binding listeners

Start Tor control only after successful P2P binding so a failed bind cannot race service creation with a target owned by another process.

f4d68cb50b init: reject wildcard onion binds for automatic Tor

Reject wildcard onion binds while automatic onion service creation is enabled because incoming connections report a concrete local address that does not match the configured wildcard.

Co-authored-by: Vasil Dimov <vd@FreeBSD.org>
Co-authored-by: JP <jeanpablo.jp@hotmail.com>

67420f758a tor: skip automatic onion services without a dedicated bind

With normal `-bind` options (but no `=onion` bind), retain the Tor controller for outbound proxy discovery but skip automatic incoming service creation, warning after authentication instead of forwarding incoming Tor connections to a normal P2P listener.

This preserves explicit listener selection without refusing startup on non-Tor nodes, while retaining the default onion listener when no `-bind` is supplied.

Co-authored-by: Vasil Dimov <vd@FreeBSD.org>
Co-authored-by: JP <jeanpablo.jp@hotmail.com>

281c9d9850 doc: explain Tor startup without an onion bind
